  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="78c0f0c2-bda5-533f-9eb6-92bf61dcd493" activityNameId="117cc466-15fa-533c-a445-c697154315ee" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Indium, at regional storage</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Indium, at regional storage
The module describes the primary production of indium metal (99.999%, 5N) on a European average. No secondary sources from post consumer scrap are consid-ered. Only the most important source of indium raw material, the hydrometallurgical zinc operations, is reflected with the dataset. This dataset is based on the respec-tive flow from multi-output module "smelting, primary zinc production". This dataset is not to be used when indium is a substantial part of the system modelled, viz. for comparisons of special solder pastes.;
CAS number: 007440-74-6; 
Formula: In; 
UUID: be4379d0-79c5-3334-b62c-91e40c407195
The module includes the production of indium from zinc extraction operations. Infrastructure and transports to Europe are considered. Most process specific emissions are missing.
Location: This module represents the production of primary indium on a European average. The inventory however is compiled with global average data, e.g. for zinc-production.
Technology: Indium containing residues from hydrometallurgical zinc operations are leached. Subsequent solvent extraction and precipitation of sponge indium. Indium cathodes are cast and electrorefined, followed by vacuum refining to obtain 5N quality. Solvent-extraction and electrowinning has been extrapolated from copper refining.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 480 t in 2006
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_be4379d0-79c5-3334-b62c-91e40c407195.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">RER</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location: This module represents the production of primary indium on a European average. The inventory however is compiled with global average data, e.g. for zinc-production.</text>
        </comment>
      </geography>
      <technology>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Technology: Indium containing residues from hydrometallurgical zinc operations are leached. Subsequent solvent extraction and precipitation of sponge indium. Indium cathodes are cast and electrorefined, followed by vacuum refining to obtain 5N quality. Solvent-extraction and electrowinning has been extrapolated from copper refining.</text>
        </comment>
      </technology>
      <timePeriod startDate="2005-01-01" endDate="2005-12-31" isDataValidForEntirePeriod="true">
        <comment>
